Third party material redistributed in this repository
-----------------------------------------------------

internal/golden/corpus holds recorded ICS protocol responses used to test the
decoders without hardware. Some of those recordings were taken from published
packet captures rather than produced here, and they are redistributed under the
terms of the collections they came from.

ICS-Security-Tools
  https://github.com/ITI/ICS-Security-Tools
  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0).
  Individual response frames were extracted from captures in the pcaps
  directory of that repository. Every fixture derived from it names the file it
  came from in its references and names CC-BY-4.0 in its license field, so the
  attribution stays attached to the bytes it covers.

Fixtures marked with the provenance "constructed" are not redistributed
material. Their bytes are derived here from the behaviour of the open source
emulators they cite, and internal/golden re-derives them on every test run
rather than copying anything from those projects.
